# Wingman

Wingman is a personal, cross-repository team brain for building software and
cloud systems. It holds the shared working agreement and links to each
repository's own authoritative instructions.

## Start here

1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) before working in this repository.
2. Review [team.yaml](team.yaml) for known context and explicit open questions.
3. Use [brain/context](brain/context/) to find each repository's purpose and
   existing guidance.
4. Review the [repo layout](brain/LAYOUT.md) and [two-week setup plan](brain/SETUP.md).

The brain is intentionally conservative: repository-specific instructions and
technical controls remain authoritative; this repository adds shared context
and proposes human approval for consequential changes. See
[constitution.md](constitution.md).

## Maintenance

Update shared guidance through a reviewed change to this repository. Keep
unknown policies in [brain/questions.md](brain/questions.md), and remove them
only when confirmed. Review lightly each month and more deeply each quarter.
